  "solution": {
    "notes": [
      "The cumulative sum is always the sum of nums[0] through nums[i] when position i is updated.",
      "Under the constraints, the largest possible absolute running sum is 10^9, which fits in a signed 32-bit integer."
    ],
    "approach": "Scan the array from left to right while maintaining a cumulative sum. Add each current value to the cumulative sum and store that sum at the same position. This produces the running-sum array in place.",
    "editorial": {
      "better": {
        "complexity": "O(n) time and O(n) auxiliary/output space.",
        "description": "Maintain one cumulative sum while scanning left to right and write each cumulative value into a separate result array. Each element is processed once."
      },
      "optimal": {
        "complexity": "O(n) time and O(1) auxiliary space.",
        "description": "Maintain a cumulative sum and overwrite nums[i] with that sum as the array is scanned. No second result array is required."
      },
      "bruteForce": {
        "complexity": "O(n^2) time and O(n) output space.",
        "description": "For every position i, separately sum nums[0] through nums[i] and append the result. This directly follows the definition but repeats earlier additions."
      }
    },
    "timeComplexity": "O(n)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) auxiliary space",
    "code": {
      "Python3": "class Solution:\n    def runningSum(self, nums):\n        total = 0\n        for i, value in enumerate(nums):\n            total += value\n            nums[i] = total\n        return nums",
      "Java": "import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\nclass Solution {\n    public int[] runningSum(int[] nums) {\n        int total = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {\n            total += nums[i];\n            nums[i] = total;\n        }\n        return nums;\n    }\n}",
      "C++": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nclass Solution {\npublic:\n    vector<int> runningSum(vector<int>& nums) {\n        long long total = 0;\n        for (int& x : nums) {\n            total += x;\n            x = static_cast<int>(total);\n        }\n        return nums;\n    }\n};",
      "JavaScript": "var runningSum = function(nums) {\n    let total = 0;\n    for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {\n        total += nums[i];\n        nums[i] = total;\n    }\n    return nums;\n}",
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nstatic int* parse_int_array(const char* s, int* out_size) {\n    const char* p = strchr(s, '[');\n    if (!p) { *out_size = 0; return NULL; }\n    p++;\n    int cap = 16, n = 0;\n    int* a = (int*)malloc(cap * sizeof(int));\n    while (*p && *p != ']') {\n        while (*p == ' ' || *p == ',') p++;\n        if (*p == ']') break;\n        char* end;\n        long v = strtol(p, &end, 10);\n        if (end == p) { p++; continue; }\n        if (n == cap) { cap *= 2; a = (int*)realloc(a, cap * sizeof(int)); }\n        a[n++] = (int)v;\n        p = end;\n    }\n    *out_size = n;\n    return a;\n}\n\n/**\n * Note: The returned array is malloced; caller should free it.\n */\nint* runningSum(int* nums, int numsSize, int* returnSize) {\n    int* result = (int*)malloc((size_t)numsSize * sizeof(int));\n    int sum = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < numsSize; ++i) {\n        sum += nums[i];\n        result[i] = sum;\n    }\n    *returnSize = numsSize;\n    return result;\n}"
    }
  },
